A1. The nut that holds the steering wheel. ~ DRIVER
A6. To set upon (nothing to do with eggs). ~ ATTACK
A11. Melancholy Iron. ~ SAD
A12. A mouse trap. ~ CAT
A14. Any straight shooter has to do this. ~ AIM
A15. In this or that manner. ~ SO
A17. You might talk over this with your friends. ~ TELEPHONE
A20. Indefinite article. ~ AN
A21. Ejaculation of the inebriate. ~ HIC
A23. This means nothing at all. ~ NIL
A24. Say it with flowers if you like—but don't say it with this. ~ INK
A25. These are grown in the wide open spaces according to certain novelists. ~ MEN
A26. Measures of length. ~ ELLS
A28. Quite enough to make a fellow go up in the air. ~ PLANE
A30. This, if full, would be considered a wise crack by any bad yegg. ~ SAFE
A31. A slippery fish. ~ ELL
A33. You've got to do this to understand anything. ~ SEE
A34. To steep. ~ RET
A35. Indispensable on all auto trips. ~ MOTOR
A37. How could the Romans have done this—if they had loaned their ears to Brutus. ~ HEARD
A39. This is a blow—but a gentle one. ~ TAP
A40. This made Caesar cross. ~ RUBICON
A41. A promise that's often broken. ~ IOU
A42. A heap of stones which marks the spot. ~ CAIRN
A44. These are served in jail. ~ TERMS
A47. Attempt. ~ TRY
A48. A hand-out. ~ ALM
A50. This wins the women. ~ WOO
A52. A fur jumper. ~ HARE
A54. A literary composition. ~ ESSAY
A56. Hold-up places. ~ INNS
A58. Epoch. ~ ERA
A59. Lots of these in Horizontal 58 (abbr.). ~ YRS
A60. You lose this when you stand up. ~ LAP
A62. In addition, besides, further, still or what have you? ~ YET
A63. Something never left (abbr.). ~ RT
A64. This fellow has to take care to do his business. ~ CARETAKER
A67. This means us. ~ WE
A68. What Mr. Babbitt likes to go around in (not a Kiddie Car). ~ PAR
A69. To speak. ~ SAY
A70. What you get if you put two and two together. ~ SUM
A72. What the American does for his freedom. ~ YEARNS
A73. It takes effort to do this. ~ ATTAIN

D1. These play a big part in the Morse code. ~ DASHES
D2. Part of the verb to be. ~ IS
D3. This holds a lot of liquor. ~ VAT
D4. Where the first loud speaker was made. ~ EDEN
D5. Found in every family tree. ~ SAP
D7. A storage place for gas. ~ TANK
D8. Good for a neck. ~ TIE
