D10. A doggie home. ~ KENNEL
D12. Those who live in these can't go out nights. ~ CELLS
D13. Possessive pronoun in old Philadelphia. ~ THINE
D16. This is smooth, though often unrefined. ~ OIL
D18. This meets with a kiss. ~ LIP
D19. This is odd. ~ ONE
D20. An organization that went on a European tour a few years ago (init.). ~ AEF
D22. This lady made her Mark. ~ CLEOPATRA
D25. A united state. ~ MATRIMONY
D27. Any old hen is apt to do this. ~ SLT
D29. Set 'em up on the house and get the air. ~ AERIALS
D30. Something between Rome and Carthage at the time of Caesar. ~ SEA
D32. A type of English wagon. ~ LORRY
D34. Do this to your Judge subscription (adv.) ~ RENEW
D35. Call a Scotchman this and you won't be far wrong. ~ MAC
D36. You don't have to do this to be "fast." ~ RUN
D37. This kind of dog never bites. ~ HOT
D38. Distinguished Occidental Society (init.). ~ DOS
D43. The anger of crossword puzzles. ~ IRE
D45. French for King. ~ ROI
D46. George did not cut the tree down for this. ~ CHERRY
D48. People who disagree with you. ~ ASSES
D49. A peninsula on the other side of the world. ~ MALAY
D51. Like the cow's tail, this is always behind. ~ ASTERN
D53. Found in very few artists' studios. ~ ART
D54. A very human thing to do. ~ ERR
D55. A hairy animal of Central Asia. ~ YAK
